    {
      "case": "1957 first Poultry Book number and bookseller confusion",
      "source_ids": [
        "DCP-LETT-1957"
      ],
      "requirement": "Preserve Darwin’s contemporary statement that he has obtained only the first number of the Poultry Book he then believed relevant. Later apparatus/bookseller identification is a separate layer and cannot be used as knowledge of the completed work or silently rewrite the body. The Finnikin/Turner query, Dorking observations and possible Cochin cross remain questions or qualified observations, not settled breed conclusions.",
      "exact_source_evidence": [
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-1957",
          "body_paragraph": 3,
          "quote": "Would you object at any time to put in Cottage Gardener, a query whether any one in England has Finnikin or Turner Pigeons?",
          "char_start": 0,
          "char_end": 123,
          "source_sha256": "d96eba33cde5bd173223e283d0c66180e6814556746d6fbab601ce54a876a945",
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div/div[1]/div[2]/p[4]"
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-1957",
          "body_paragraph": 4,
          "quote": "the good woman assured me that this was their general, but not quite invariable characteristic.",
          "char_start": 287,
          "char_end": 382,
          "source_sha256": "d96eba33cde5bd173223e283d0c66180e6814556746d6fbab601ce54a876a945",
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div/div[1]/div[2]/p[5]"
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-1957",
          "body_paragraph": 5,
          "quote": "I have only got as yet 1st nor of the Poultry Book, so do not know yet how you are getting on.",
          "char_start": 0,
          "char_end": 94,
          "source_sha256": "d96eba33cde5bd173223e283d0c66180e6814556746d6fbab601ce54a876a945",
